# Every feature flag, declared once, here.
#
# A module is gated by NOT BEING BUILT - protocore_add_module() returns early when its GATE is
# off - rather than by compiling to an empty translation unit. The option is also passed to the
# compiler, because a flag decides more than whether a module exists: it selects arms inside
# modules that are built either way, and the Arduino shim has no source selection at all and
# reaches these only as -D flags out of its build_opt.h.
#
# GENERATED ONCE from the config headers' own defaults, then maintained here.

# Hardware capabilities a module's gate can name. OFF by default: the host has none of
# them, and a part that does states it. Declared so a compound gate resolves from a real
# option rather than from a variable that happens to be undefined.
